# job-search

- **Stack:** Cloudflare Worker + D1 + TypeScript. Entry `src/index.ts`; orchestration is **Durable Object + Queue** (`src/orchestration/`), and batch job processing lives in `src/pipeline/runPipeline.ts`.
- **Job sources:** `getEnabledProviders` in `src/providers/index.ts`. IDs: `linkedin_jobs` (Fantastic Jobs **`/active-jb-24h`** by default, per-country rotation + US throttle + chunked page fetch), `jsearch` (legacy RapidAPI JSearch).
- **Employment type:** `normalizeEmploymentType` / `canonicalizeEmploymentType` (`src/providers/lib/employmentTypeCanonical.ts`, `providerFieldSemantics.ts`) — optional **country hint** (ISO2 or full name from `searchCountries`) for language rules **before** `franc-min`; if no match, **franc fallback** (no translation API). LinkedIn/JSearch/Jobs API pass country where available. **`runPlannedSearchProvider` `merge`** signature: **`(row, detail, ctx: PlannedSearchContext)`** — use `ctx.country.iso2` / `fullName` when merging rows.
- **Dashboard:** `public/dashboard.html` + `src/dashboard/api.ts` (settings, logs, job list, **`GET /api/pipeline-status`**, **`GET /api/statistics`**). D1 `app_logs` / `app_settings`. UI labels Applied/Reject; DB/API still `accepted`/`denied`. **`POST /api/jobs/:id/restore`** — from Applied/Reject to active, or from **filtered** to active as Low (`low_priority_review`). Bulk: **`POST /api/jobs/bulk-accept`**, **`bulk-deny`**, **`bulk-restore`**, **`bulk-delete`** `{ ids }` (no `confirm()` on delete). Expanded job **Pipeline & extraction** = only **`ingestionRequestParams`** (HTTP request path/query as sent—`src/dashboard/ingestionFacts.ts`, `src/lib/httpRequestParamsRecord.ts`), not response payload fields. **Statistics — title↔query health:** UI is a **single summary line** of mean score per vendor (`Vendor: X.X, …`); scorer and API live in `src/metrics/titleQueryHealth/`, `src/db/titleQueryHealthStats.ts`; tests: **`npm run test:title-query-health`**.
- **CV (scoring + drafts):** Dashboard **Settings → CV (WORD)** → **`POST /api/settings/cv-upload`** (multipart `.docx`, mammoth) → D1 `app_settings` keys via `src/db/cvCache.ts`; runtime resolution **`getCvSources`** in `src/profile/cvSource.ts` (both text+HTML required from DB, else bundled `cv-extracted*.gen.ts`). Optional R2 `cv/latest.docx`. Repo root **`Oleg_Velikanov_CV.docx`** is gitignored; optional local **`npm run cv:extract`** refreshes bundled fallback only.
- **Scoring JSON:** **`position_summary`** — 3 sentences: **1 employer** (what they do; size/stage if in posting) + **2 role**; defaults **`src/pipeline/aiInstructionDefaults.ts`**, D1 upgrade hooks **`src/pipeline/aiInstructions.ts`**.
- **API extraction & fetch gate:** D1 `api_extraction_enabled` + **`getPipelineFetchAllowed`** (also **`PIPELINE_FETCH_ENABLED` === `"false"`** = hard kill). Triggers **`startOrResumeCoordinator`** → DO **`POST /start`**: `PATCH /api/settings` when extraction turns on, **`scheduled`** (cron), **`POST /run`**. Coordinator **`PipelineCoordinator`** enqueues one **`PIPELINE_QUEUE`** chunk at a time; consumer `handlePipelineQueue` → claim → fetch → dedupe → `processFetchedJobs` → report → pump. **`orchestrationError`** = DO/queue path, not RapidAPI vendor errors. **`processFetchedJobs`**: content-fingerprint dedupe (hash on `jobs.content_dedupe_hash`) hard-rejects duplicates before text hard filters; **Jobs API** hard-rejects when detail **`acceptingApplications === false`**.
- **Cron:** default **daily** `0 0 * * *` UTC (`wrangler.toml`); LinkedIn 24h **freeze** is D1/provider state, not the cron interval.
- **RapidAPI vendor details** (endpoints, params, credits, JSearch response shape): **`docs/rapidapi-job-providers.md`**. Rule `.cursor/rules/rapidapi-providers-reference.mdc` applies when editing provider/RapidAPI files.
- **Secrets:** `RAPIDAPI_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `REVIEW_TOKEN_SECRET` via Wrangler; never commit `.dev.vars` or keys in repo.
- **Schema changes:** new file under `migrations/`; apply with `wrangler d1 migrations apply job-search-db --remote` for production (before/with deploy).
- **Edits:** keep changes scoped; follow existing patterns in `src/db/jobs.ts`, `src/providers/linkedinJobs.ts`. Run `npm run typecheck` before deploy.
- **Deploy (mandatory for agents):** After changes under `src/`, `public/`, `wrangler.toml`, `scripts/` (when they affect build or pipeline), or `package.json`, run **`npm run deploy`** from the repo root without waiting for the user to ask—unless they explicitly said not to deploy or the session was docs-only (e.g. only `AGENTS.md` / `.md` with no runtime impact). If D1 migrations were added, apply remote migrations first, then deploy. Command: `npm run deploy` (`wrangler deploy`). Optional local **`npm run dev`** / **`npm run verify:local`** for your own debugging; production verification is the deployed Worker. Optional `npm run cv:extract` updates bundled `src/profile/`; production CV text/HTML come from dashboard upload (D1 cache) when set.

For workflows, env tables, and routes, use the project skill **job-search** (`.cursor/skills/job-search/SKILL.md`) or `AGENTS.md`.
